{
  "release": "SafeGrip-Open v1.1.0 / SafeGrip-CI",
  "purpose": "dual-expert adaptive-state proposal revision with learned prior/neural/inverse arbitration",
  "release_validation": {
    "pytest": "70 passed, 2 warnings",
    "cli_help": true,
    "synthetic_training_smoke": true,
    "primary_ablation_count": 15,
    "supplementary_optimization_ablations": 2
  },
  "verified_invariants": [
    "persistent friction state resets at trajectory-segment boundaries",
    "adaptive persistence is bounded and initialized from the configured state persistence",
    "candidate innovation is factorized into bounded direction and magnitude",
    "inverse dynamics is an explicit correction expert and is unavailable when counterfactual observability vanishes",
    "learned arbitration weights prior/neural/inverse actions and sums to one",
    "arbitration supervision uses training labels only; inference consumes no friction label",
    "scheduled teacher forcing anneals toward recursively predicted previous state",
    "counterfactual identifiability is observability evidence rather than a monotone neural-correctness gate",
    "full v1.1 uses single-scale counterfactual sensitivity; v1.0 multi-scale/linearity controls remain legacy ablations",
    "agreement is exported as direction/magnitude evidence rather than a permanent multiplicative veto",
    "final point output remains inside the conditional physical support",
    "UQ inflation can use both low observability and expert disagreement before block-max conformal calibration",
    "LiRA downloads reject zero-byte/corrupt payloads and retain public fallback behavior"
  ],
